<title>TAIWAN: First Int'l March sales up 9.2 pct.</title>
<headline>First Int'l March sales up 9.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>First International Computer Inc, Taiwan's second largest computer firm, said on Wednesday its March sales revenue rose 9.2 percent to T$2.843 billion compared to T$2.604 billion in March 1996.</p>
<p>For the first three months of 1997, First International Computer posted a sales revenue of T$7.483 billion, up 16.2 percent from the same period in 1996, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>Profit figures were not available.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
